FirmwareLab
===========

This product includes data and file-format knowledge derived from the UEFITool
project by Nikolaj Schlej, distributed under the BSD-2-Clause license:

    Copyright (c) 2015, Nikolaj Schlej
    https://github.com/LongSoft/UEFITool

Specifically:
  * firmwarelab/data/guids.csv         - the known-GUID name database
  * firmwarelab/data/jedec.csv         - SPI flash JEDEC ID -> chip name table
  * The binary layouts of UEFI volumes, FFS files, sections, NVRAM stores,
    the Intel flash descriptor, ME/CSME, microcode, FIT and Boot Guard were
    implemented with reference to UEFITool's format descriptions.

The EFI 1.1 / Tiano decompressor follows the algorithm published in the
TianoCore EDK II project (BSD-2-Clause, Intel Corporation).

FirmwareLab is an independent, from-scratch Python implementation and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the above projects.
